<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungarian Red Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hungarian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> was the armed force of the Hungarian Soviet Republic, formed in 1919 from remnants of the old army, workers' battalions and volunteers. In May and June it pushed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, where the Slovak Soviet Republic was proclaimed under its protection, and it retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murska-sobota">Murska Sobota</a> from the short-lived Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prekmurje">Prekmurje</a>. It withdrew from Slovakia under Allied pressure and collapsed before the Romanian army in early August 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungarian-red-army.jpg" alt="Hungarian Red Army" width="320" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_Flag_of_Hungary.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
